            "input": {
              "body": "Harbourline Freight Pty Ltd passes all three covenants for the test period ending 30 September 2026 on the pack figures, and no covenant is on watch.\n\nNet leverage: 2.07x tested against a 3.50x maximum, headroom 40.9%. Calculated as (total debt 19,850 less cash 3,420) divided by TTM EBITDA 7,940.\n\nInterest cover: 6.06x tested against a 2.00x minimum, headroom 203.1%. Calculated as TTM EBITDA 7,940 divided by TTM interest expense 1,310.\n\nMinimum liquidity: 7,420 tested against a 2,500 minimum ($'000), headroom 196.8%. Calculated as cash 3,420 plus undrawn revolver 4,000.\n\nThe compliance certificate agrees with the tested results on all three covenants; no disagreements were found.\n\nReview issues:\n- Balance sheet total assets at 30 Sep 2026 is printed as 34,050, but its lines add to 34,140 (difference 90).\n- Commentary says no new borrowings were drawn, yet borrowings rose from 19,250 at 30 June to 19,850 at 30 September (up 600).\n\nRecommended action: Analyst to confirm the total assets figure with the borrower and to reconcile the 600 increase in borrowings against the commentary before sign-off. No covenant action is indicated on the reported figures."
