            "text": "The September 2026 monitoring run for Harbourline Freight is saved as a note awaiting analyst sign-off. On the pack figures, all three covenants pass.\n\n| Covenant | Tested | Limit | Headroom | Certificate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Net leverage | 2.07x | max 3.50x | 40.9% | Agrees |\n| Interest cover | 6.06x | min 2.00x | 203.1% | Agrees |\n| Minimum liquidity | $7,420k | min $2,500k | 196.8% | Agrees |\n\nAll six required figures were accepted on the first submission, and the three certificate claims were accepted as well.\n\nThe test returned two review issues, both included in the note:\n- **Total assets:** the balance sheet prints $34,050k at 30 September, but its lines add to $34,140k, a $90k difference.\n- **Borrowings:** the commentary says no new borrowings were drawn, yet total borrowings rose by $600k from 30 June to 30 September. The system did not flag this, so I added it from my own comparison of the balance sheet with the commentary.\n\nThe note recommends the analyst confirm the total assets figure and reconcile the borrowings increase before sign-off."
